3194139535271 true] [17592186341061 1100 "Find the horizontal asymptote of the function $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{5}+1}{4{x}^{3}-x+1}.$" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341061 1113 #uuid "677d5738-cb69-509e-8934-2dc2fbf03ad1" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341061 1145 "The horizontal asymptote is $y={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x).$ To find the horizontal asymptote, we apply the usual procedure of dividing the numerator and denominator by the highest power of $x$ in the denominator, which is ${x}^{3}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{x}^{5}+1}{4{x}^{3}-x+1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{x}{{x}^{3}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{({x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})}{(4-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{({x}^{2}+0)}{(4-0+0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{x}^{2} \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe limit does not come out to a finite number. Therefore, there is no horizontal asymptote." 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341063 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341064 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341065 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341066 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341067 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1041 "selection" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341065 13194139535271 true] [17592186341062 1110 #uuid "921027f6-007e-5682-b582-67652c527968" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341063 1034 "y=\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341063 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535271 true] [17592186341063 1111 #uuid "9166d501-5363-5134-b4ae-cfa72506f7cd" 13194139535271 true] [17592186341064 1034 "y=0" 13194139535271 true] [175